# Git commits (this repo)

Commits from the agent must use the GitHub account **brimmann** so history matches the remote owner.

Do **not** use the default shell identity (`rashid@DESKTOP-…` or ad hoc `rashid@users.noreply.github.com` unless it matches below).

## Author (required on every commit)

Always pass identity via `-c` flags (do not change global or local `git config`):

```bash
git -c user.name="Rashid" \
    -c user.email="58560473+brimmann@users.noreply.github.com" \
    commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Your message here.

EOF
)"
```

- **Name:** `Rashid` (GitHub display name)
- **Email:** `58560473+brimmann@users.noreply.github.com` (GitHub noreply for login `brimmann`, links commits to that account)

If the user asks to use their public email instead, use `rashidstanikzai.net@gmail.com` with the same name.

## Push

After commit, push with normal `git push` (GitHub CLI auth is already configured for `brimmann/red-deer-jobs-design`).
